 app/services_sarma/

All logic (your “brains”):
 --> text_expansion_service_sa.py → expand complaint text (optional)

--> text_severity_service_sa.py → urgency/impact/frequency → text severity
--> ml_prediction_service_sa.py → ML suggestion (supporting only)
--> osm_fetch_service_sa.py → real OSM fetch using Overpass API (dynamic)
--> gis_summary_builder_sa.py → makes officer-friendly GIS summary line
--> gis_usage_service_sa.py + gis_usage_helpers_sa.py → Hybrid GIS score calculation
--> recurring_detection_service_sa.py → recurring count + is_recurring
--> recurring_severity_service_sa.py → recurring severity score
--> priority_scoring_service_sa.py → final score = Text + GIS + Recurring
--> priority_level_service_sa.py → score → level (High/Medium/Low)
--> track_decision_service_sa.py → Planning vs Operational
--> officer_output_service_sa.py → builds final officer JSON (ordered + explainable)


4) Required packages (install list)

Create a virtual environment (recommended):

Windows (PowerShell)
python -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\activate


Install dependencies:

pip install fastapi uvicorn sqlalchemy pydantic pydantic-settings requests
pip install scikit-learn pandas joblib
pip install geopy


Optional (only if you use .env nicely):

pip install python-dotenv

5) How to run the backend

Go inside the backend root (where app/ exists), then:

uvicorn app.main_sarma:app --reload


Now open:

Swagger UI: http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs

6) How to use the API
A) Submit complaint

POST /complaints/submit

Example JSON:

{
  "category": "road",
  "text": "There is no proper bridge here. Very dangerous during rainy season.",
  "expand_text": true,
  "location_link": "https://maps.app.goo.gl/HwWQsFdGHa7C8siv6"
}

B) Officer view

GET /officer/complaint/1

It returns:
summary (priority level/score)
location link
why_this_priority list
gis details_for_popup
recurring info
AI suggestion note (supporting only)
track decision